1
00:00:04,647 --> 00:00:12,927
Record a diagnosis — Patients ▸ Diagnoses — Code it properly once, and the claim, the chart and the portal all agree.

2
00:00:18,144 --> 00:00:25,121
Patients ▸ Diagnoses is every coded problem across the practice, not just one chart.

3
00:00:25,121 --> 00:00:40,386
Filter by patient or by status to answer the questions that actually come up — who is active, what is chronic, what resolved.

4
00:00:40,386 --> 00:00:47,002
Give it the name a clinician would say out loud.

5
00:00:47,002 --> 00:00:58,281
Now the part that matters: search the ICD-10 code. Typing one from memory is how claims get denied.

6
00:00:58,281 --> 00:01:06,394
Picking from the list guarantees the code and its description agree — payers check exactly that.

7
00:01:06,394 --> 00:01:12,653
Severity is clinical judgement, and it travels with the diagnosis.

8
00:01:12,653 --> 00:01:32,292
Active is happening now. Chronic is ongoing and managed. Resolved is over — and marking it so is what keeps the problem list honest.

9
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:40,698
Saved once, used everywhere — it justifies the claim, sits on the chart, and appears in the patient’s portal.

10
00:01:42,193 --> 00:01:58,603
What you just did

11
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:08,233
